# DECOMPOSITION.in - anode_physical_A100: anode_physical with the SEI
# ACCELERATION FACTOR A_SEI = 100 applied to the three electrolyte-reduction
# channels (FSI, SFO, SOL, SOL2). Plating and stripping (BV block) are NOT
# accelerated. Purpose: SEI morphology studies; each simulated
# cycle deposits the SEI of ~100 physical cycles (docs/KINETICS_TABLE.md, sec. 7).
# Basis of the reference values: docs/KINETICS_TABLE.md
# format: <NAME> <nChannels> then per channel: sigma k0 Ea alpha E0
# Plating / PlatingSEI: IGNORED in anode_kinetics bv (Butler-Volmer block in
# PARAMETERS.in supplies both). Kept for the parser.
Plating 1
1 1E-4 0.000 0.0 -3.04
PlatingSEI 1
1 1E-4 0.000 0.0 -3.04
# ---- electrolyte reduction at the Li surface -------------------------------
# LiFSI (FSI) and F5DEE (SOL) reduction on Li are barrierless (LICET, Tan et
# al. JACS 2024, p. 11714), so their rate is electron-transfer limited and,
# without an explicit tunnelling attenuation through the SEI [P], cannot be
# taken as the bare j0 (it would consume the electrolyte at once; Boyle 2020
# shows the SEI-limited effective j0 is ~100x below the kinetic one).
# CE-ANCHORED CHOICE: side-reaction events per plating event = (1 - CE)/CE
# with CE = 0.998 (Yu 2022, LiFSI/F5DEE Li||Cu, 99.74 to 99.90 %) -> 2.0e-3.
# The side-reaction k0 are set so that the OBSERVED event ratio (side events /
# plating events) equals 2.0e-3, keeping the original network's internal
# ratios SFO = 0.01 FSI, SOL = 0.02 FSI (Perez-Beltran 2024, relative).
# Anchoring accounts for candidate multiplicity: the BV plating weight is
# k_bv x N_growth (161 growth sites in the 10x10x30 box at half-cycle 45)
# while FSI / SOL decomposition weigh k x (salt or solvent sites touching Li0:
# 2 and 16 to 20). Solving side/plating = 2e-3 with the original SOL:FSI event
# ratio 0.13 gives k_FSI = 19, k_SOL = 0.25, k_SFO = 0.19 s^-1 per adjacent
# site. Note k_FSI is of the order of k_bv itself: FSI reduction at the
# interface is fast per molecule (barrierless, Tan 2024) and the high CE comes
# from the scarcity of salt at the interface. Values are geometry-dependent
# (through N_growth / N_adjacent) and are re-derived per box size.
# Tag [V-derived, CE-anchored]. NOTE: at this physical ratio the SEI formed in
# a 40 x 40 A patch is a few sites per cycle; morphology studies of the SEI
# need an explicit, reported acceleration factor on these three k0 (the
# original engine's 1e-4 : 1e-4 ratio corresponds to an acceleration of ~500).
FSI 1
1 1900 0.000 0.0 -3.04
SFO 1
1 19 0.000 0.0 -3.04
SOL 1
1 25 0.000 0.0 -3.04
# F5DEE on Li2O (SOL2): candidates are solvent sites touching an O (Li2O)
# site. Same CE-anchored prefactor as SOL x A_SEI (25 s^-1) with the Tan 2024
# DFT/NEB barrier 0.364 eV as the relative attenuation of the Li2O route vs
# the barrierless Li route: k = 0.25 exp(-0.364/kT) = 1.8e-7 s^-1 [V-derived].
# The kT/h prefactor used before (6.2e12 -> 4.5e6 s^-1 per site) is an
# elementary-step rate, not an effective electrode rate: in the full cell it
# made every O site an inexhaustible F5DEE sink (see docs/CHANGELOG.md).
SOL2 1
1 25 0.364 0.0 -3.04
